# Headless LOK dev build for the MS Word clone (Boundary A engine).
#
# Tree is PRISTINE LibreOffice @ commit 1f1121d1 (re-vendored 2026-05-29, replacing the
# old reskin's hacked/stripped tree). Slimming to a Writer-focused engine is done HERE via
# supported configure flags -- NOT by deleting modules, which is exactly what broke the
# old tree (dangling refs to opencl/helplinker/etc.). See docs/engine-revendor-impact.md.
#
# OOM-safe caps for the 15 GB box are load-bearing: no LTO, no mergelibs, parallelism 8.

# --- headless: no desktop/UI integration (we only render via LOK tiles) ---
--disable-gui
--disable-gtk3
--disable-gtk4
--disable-qt5
--disable-qt6
--disable-kf5
--disable-dbus
--disable-gio
--disable-randr
--disable-cups
--disable-gstreamer-1-0

# --- cut subsystems not needed for Writer layout / shaping / .docx I/O ---
--without-java
--without-junit
--without-help
--without-myspell-dicts
--disable-odk
--disable-online-update
# NOTE: do NOT --disable-database-connectivity — svx's form layer links against the
# connectivity/dbtools library, so disabling it breaks libsvxcorelo.so (a core module).
# We still drop the heavy SDBC backends below; that part is cleanly optional.
--disable-firebird-sdbc
--disable-postgresql-sdbc
--disable-report-builder
--disable-lpsolve
--disable-lotuswordpro
--disable-scripting-beanshell
--disable-scripting-javascript
--disable-python
--disable-opencl

# --- build shape: product build, no packaging, en-US only, capped parallelism ---
--enable-release-build
--with-package-format=no
--with-lang=en-US
--with-parallelism=8
--with-vendor=cua-bench
